{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792234805,"nonce":"9/l7Asql085NsPYqssL7Z+D4fA4=","title":"Cranelift tier: make it strong via MIR passes so LLVM is needed only for the hottest functions","message":"User direction (2026-10-17): the Cranelift tier should be highly optimized through MIR passes; LLVM only for hot-most functions. This is also the path to beating hxcpp on cold `rayzor run`.\n\nCold NUC measurements at 6b4fb34d (fresh process, hxcpp binary vs `rayzor run`):\n- fib: 798 ms vs hxcpp 110\n- deltablue: 71 ms vs 8\n- spectralnorm: 425 ms vs 162\n- `--llvm` is slower again: it does a whole-program LLVM compile on top of the Cranelift one.\n\nWarm CI comparison, Cranelift vs LLVM:\n- spectralnorm 566 vs 198\n- fannkuchredux 629 vs 320\n- fasta 417 vs 282\n- fib 285 vs 245\n\nFindings (code map, file:line as of 6b4fb34d):\n1. Array loads are never hoisted. Every `a[i]` reloads len@8, flags@32 and data, with two branches (ir/mir/field/access.rs:1396; lvalue.rs:1280).\n   - MIR LICM refuses to hoist any Load if the loop has any call or store (optimization.rs:1031).\n   - BCE is dead: it only matches `haxe_array_get_ptr`, which lowering no longer emits (bounds_check_elimination.rs:64).\n   - Cranelift loads carry no readonly flag and no alias region (instruction_lowering.rs:502, 518).\n   - This is the main suspect for spectralnorm and fannkuchredux.\n2. There is no MIR-tier differentiation. `OptimizationTier::mir_opt_level()` (tiered_backend.rs:440) is never called. Baseline, Standard and Optimized all emit the same O2 MIR at Cranelift \"speed\", and the Beadie adapters run no MIR passes.\n3. Hotness is invisible inside JIT code. `record_call` only fires from `execute_function`, i.e. the entry. Direct calls between JIT'd functions are never counted, so `rayzor run` never promotes. OSR probes exist at loop headers, but helpers are built only for a bead root, so they never arm. Recursion has no OSR at all.\n4. Stack-trace push/pop is a C call on every function call unless `--release`, and frame pointers are always on.\n5. There is no default vectorization, no strength reduction or IV widening, and unrolling only covers bodies of 32 instructions or fewer.\n6. Cold start does a whole-program Cranelift compile plus O2 MIR before main. `--llvm` and `.rzb` add work rather than replacing it.\nEnv aids: RAYZOR_DUMP_CLIF=\u003cpattern\u003e, RAYZOR_PROFILE_LOAD, RAYZOR_PROFILE_COMPILE, RAYZOR_PROFILE_TIER_EVENTS, RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES.","files":null}]}